+## Embedding native extensions in one addon
+
+Rust hosts can link `gpuix-native` as an rlib and call
+`native_extensions::install(fn(&mut CustomElementRegistry))` once, before any
+view or registry is created. Default registries invoke this installer after
+built-in factories. Duplicate or late installation returns an error. An empty
+registry also seals startup, but intentionally does not install defaults.
+
+The facade re-exports `CustomElement`, `CustomElementFactory`,
+`CustomRenderContext`, `CustomElementRegistry`, `custom_surface`, `EventCallback`,
+the opaque `GpuixView`, and the exact `gpui` crate used by the renderer. Factories
+and elements are created on the rendering thread; they are not required to be
+`Send`. Give surfaces stable host-derived named IDs, call `custom_surface` for
+style/event/bounds instrumentation, and paint text through `ctx.text` or
+`ctx.chrome_text`. The host owns explicit startup order, not static constructors.
+
+Build the host addon in release mode and set `NAPI_RS_NATIVE_LIBRARY_PATH` to its
+absolute canonical path before importing `@gpuix/native`. Application bindings
+must load that same file. Loading a second addon creates separate native state.
+This extension API does not add multi-window support.
+
